// mg_restrict — transfer a fine-grid field to the next coarser grid by 2^d averaging
// (full-weighting-ish). Dispatched over the COARSE grid: coarse cell c gathers the 2^d fine
// cells at 2c + {0,1}^d. r_fine = set 2, r_coarse = set 3.
//
// DIMENSION-GENERIC (solver-ledger.md §7d). 2x2 in 2D, 2x2x2 in 3D, from one file: the
// gather set is ST_BIT_OFFSET over ST_CORNERS and the divisor is ST_CORNERS.
//
// The 2D path is BIT-IDENTICAL to the hand-written version it replaces. The old form was
// 0.25*(((a+b)+c)+d); the loop accumulates from 0.0 in the same order (0.0+a == a exactly)
// and divides by 4.0 instead of multiplying by 0.25 — both exact powers of two. That matters:
// the residual column is the regression oracle for this whole refactor, so restriction had
// to stay exact rather than merely equivalent.
//
// Host must supply, before this body: #version, local_size, the two r32f images (r_fine @
// set 2, r_coarse @ set 3), and a push constant named `pc` with `coarse_size` then
// `fine_size` (vec2 each in 2D, vec4 each in 3D).

void main() {
    ST_IVEC c = ST_CELL();
    ST_IVEC cmx = ST_EXTENT(pc.coarse_size) - ST_IVEC(1);
    if (any(greaterThan(c, cmx))) {
        return;
    }
    ST_IVEC fmx = ST_EXTENT(pc.fine_size) - ST_IVEC(1);
    ST_IVEC f = c * 2;

    float acc = 0.0;
    for (int k = 0; k < ST_CORNERS; k++) {
        acc += imageLoad(r_fine, min(f + ST_BIT_OFFSET(k), fmx)).r;
    }
    imageStore(r_coarse, c, vec4(acc / float(ST_CORNERS), 0.0, 0.0, 0.0));
}
